Z||000003||c m west||06-14-2001||10:14 PM||||Polyurathane is one sugesstion, however if you want to step up to the plate, we offer Delrin bushings for the Fiero. Delrin is self lubricating, offers no defflection which is constant with both poly and rubber, and there will not be any annoying squeaking that is common with polyurathane.<P>  Our bushings are greasable and and are currently in stock, to veiw them check out our website<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||06-15-2001||03:12 AM||||Thanks CM West. I'll have to check more into that material. I need to know where to get everything though because i don't know what all to change. Ray i have been in hiding after my ex and i split. Spent alot of time driving the vette and letting the fieros sit. now i am dieing to drive my fieros again.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||06-15-2001||07:06 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.suspension.com</A>  now offers a complete package including all of the urethane bushings as well as new ball joints and tie rod ends.||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||06-15-2001||07:40 AM||||i ordered all of my poly bushings through NOPI... saved a ton of money over the fierostore.  they are drop shipped from the parent company to prothane, so there is not problem with them being "the real thing" as so many people have feared!  hell, they are even in the same packaging as the fierostore pics!<P>i got cradle, both front and rear control arms delivered for $100, or less.  if you do a search for NOPI, bushings, and my name, you will get all the part numbers.  believe me, you need the part numbers to deal with NOPI (they are less than enthusiastic about dealing with anything that isn't made in Japan)!<P>email me if you have any specific questions.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000007||MoneypitGT||06-16-2001||09:09 PM||||Call prothane direct,1-888-prothane. I picked up a full set for dirt compared to anyone else.<BR> Chris <P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||14
